          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em complex Hopf fibration
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Hopf31"}> Hopf (1931)
            \&amp;rbrack; is a canonical nontrivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            whose total space is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^1 \hookrightarrow S^3 \to S^2
                  \\,.
          %p
            Its canonically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basic+line+bundle+on+the+2-sphere"} basic line bundle on the 2-sphere
          %p This we discuss below in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#DefinitionFor3Sphere"} On the 3-sphere
          %p More generally, there are four Hopf fibrations, on the 1-sphere, the 3-sphere, the 7-sphere and the 15-sphere, respectively. This we discuss in
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#OnAllFourSpheres"} On the 1-sphere, 3-sphere, 7-sphere and 15-sphere
              \.
          %h2#DefinitionFor3Sphere On the 3-sphere
          %h3#HomotopyTheoreticCharacterization Homotopy-theoretic characterization
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{Z},2) \simeq B S^1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_2(K(\mathbb{Z},2)) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means that there is, up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi : S^2 \to K(\mathbb{Z},2)
                  \\,,
          %p
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ±
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\phi] \in \pi_2(K(\mathbb{Z},2)) = \pm 1 \in \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            As any map into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{Z},2)
            this classifies a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            over its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^1 &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; S^3
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; S^2
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp;
                  B S^1 \simeq K(\mathbb{Z},2)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In other words, the Hopf fibration is the
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
          %h3#realization_via_the_complex_numbers Realization via the complex numbers
          %p
            An explicit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            presenting the Hopf fibration may be obtained as follows. Identify
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^3
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\big\{
                  (z_0, z_1) \in \mathbb{C}\times \mathbb{C}
                  \\,\big\vert\,
                  {|z_0|}^2 + {|z_1|}^2 = 1
                  \\big\}
                  \\;=\;
                  S(\mathbb{C}^2)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂℙ
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^2
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\mathbb{C P}^1
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\mathbb{C} \sqcup \{\infty\}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to S^2
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (z_0, \,z_1)
                  \\;\mapsto\;
                  \\frac{z_0}{z_1}
          %p
            gives the Hopf fibration. (Thus, the Hopf fibration is the circle bundle naturally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            with the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+line+bundle"} canonical line bundle
          %p Alternatively, if we identify
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^2
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\big\{
                  (z, x) \in \mathbb{C} \times \mathbb{R}
                  \\,\big\vert\,
                  {|z|}^2 + x^2 = 1
                  \\big\}
                  \\,=\,
                  S(\mathbb{C} \times \mathbb{R})
          %p
            and identify this presentation of the 2-sphere with the complex projective line via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stereographic+projection"} stereographic projection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (z_0, z_1)
                  \\;\mapsto\;
                  \\big(
                  2 z_0 \overline{z_1}
                  ,\,
                  {|z_0|}^2 - {|z_1|}^2
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %h3#RealizationViaQuaternions Realization via quaternions
          %p
            Alternatively, we may regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \simeq S(\mathbb{H})
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+sphere"} unit sphere
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} im
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \simeq S\left( \mathbb{H}_{\mathrm{im}}\right)
            as the unit sphere in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℍ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msub
                              %mi ℍ
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} im
                            %mo )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi q
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi q
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi i
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mover
                            %mi q
                            %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S(\mathbb{H})
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  S\left( \mathbb{H}_{\mathrm{im}}\right)
                  \\\
                  q
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  q \cdot \mathbf{i} \cdot \overline{q}
                  }
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} im
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{i} \in S\left( \mathbb{H}_{\mathrm{im}}\right)
            is any unit imaginary quaternion.
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lyons03"} Lyons 2003 (3)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Treisman09"} Treisman 2009 §4.2
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basic+complex+line+bundle+on+the+2-sphere"} basic complex line bundle on the 2-sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "basic+complex+line+bundle+on+the+2-sphere#AsAnIndexBundle"} As an index bundle
          %h3#realization_via_the_hopf_construction Realization via the Hopf construction
          %p
            Regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 = U(1)
            as equipped with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            structure. This makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            in particular an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-space"} H-space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \to S^3 \to S^2
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+construction"} Hopf construction
            applied to this H-space.
          %h3{:id => ""}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%283%29"}> Spin(3)
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} equivariance
          %p Consider
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%283%29"} Spin(3)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
                which is induced by the defining action on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
                under the identification
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \simeq S(\mathbb{R}^3)
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-action" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%283%29"} Spin(3)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
                which is induced under the exceptional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(3) \simeq Sp(1) = U(1,\mathbb{H})
                by the canonical left action of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1,\mathbb{H})
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℍ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
                via
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 3
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℍ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \simeq S(\mathbb{H})
          %p
            Then the complex Hopf fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \overset{h_{\mathbb{C}}}{\longrightarrow} S^2
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant"} equivariant
            with respect to these
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
          %p
            A way to make the
            = succeed "-equivariance" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(3)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi fib
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi h
                                %mi ℂ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi h
                                %mi ℂ
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Spin
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi Spin
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Spin
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 3
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi Spin
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi Spin
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 3
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi Spin
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^1
                  \&amp;\overset{fib(h_{\mathbb{C}})}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  S^{3}
                  \&amp;\overset{h_{\mathbb{C}}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  S^2
                  \\\
                  \= &amp;&amp; = &amp;&amp; =
                  \\\
                  \\frac{Spin(2)}{Spin(1)}
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  \\frac{Spin(3)}{Spin(1)}
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  \\frac{Spin(3)}{Spin(2)}
                  }
          %h2#OnAllFourSpheres On the 1-sphere, 3-sphere, 7-sphere and 15-sphere
          %h3#via_norms_and_projections Via norms and projections
          %p
            For each of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebra"} normed division algebras
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbb{R}, \mathbb{C}, \mathbb{H}, \mathbb{O},
          %p
            there is a corresponding Hopf fibration of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one"} Hopf invariant one
          %p
            The total space of the fibration is the space of pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha, \beta) \in A^2
            of unit norm:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|\alpha|}^2 + {|\beta|}^2 = 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spheres"} spheres
            of dimension 1,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective
            1-space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^1(A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{2^n - 1} \to S^{2^{n-1}}
          %p
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1, 2, 3, 4
            ) which sends the pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha, \beta)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha/\beta
          %h3#via_the_hopf_construction Via the Hopf construction
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            that is an
            = succeed "-space," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0 = 1
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 = \mathbb{Z}/2
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+order+2"} group of order 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary group
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 = SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moufang+loop"} Moufang loop
            structure, then the Hopf construction produces the above four Hopf fibrations:
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0 \hookrightarrow S^1 \to S^1
              –
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+Hopf+fibration"} real Hopf fibration
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \hookrightarrow S^3 \to S^2
              –
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Hopf+fibration"} complex Hopf fibration
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \hookrightarrow S^7 \to S^4
              –
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 15
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7 \hookrightarrow S^{15} \to S^8
              –
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+Hopf+fibration"} octonionic Hopf fibration
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToStableHomotopyGroupsOfSpheres Relation to stable homotopy groups of spheres
          %p Let
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℂ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{\mathbb{C}} \in \pi_3(S^2)
            ,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℍ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{\mathbb{H}} \in \pi_7(S^4)
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 15
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{\mathbb{O}} \in \pi_{15}(S^8)
          %p
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Hopf+fibration"} complex Hopf fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+Hopf+fibration"} octonionic Hopf fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspensions"} suspensions
            are the generators of the corresponding
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mi ℂ
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ≃
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                            %mi st
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mi ℍ
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 24
                          %mo ≃
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 3
                            %mi st
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mi 𝕆
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 240
                          %mo ≃
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 7
                            %mi st
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\Sigma H_{\mathbb{C}}
                  \&amp; =
                  \\pm 1
                  \\in
                  \\mathbb{Z}_2
                  \\simeq
                  \\pi_1^{st}
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma H_{\mathbb{H}}
                  \&amp; =
                  \\pm 1
                  \\in
                  \\mathbb{Z}_{24}
                  \\simeq
                  \\pi_3^{st}
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma H_{\mathbb{O}}
                  \&amp; =
                  \\pm 1
                  \\in
                  \\mathbb{Z}_{240}
                  \\simeq
                  \\pi_7^{st}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p see also at
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} first stable homotopy group of spheres
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/third+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} third stable homotopy group of spheres
          %p
            and
            %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/224082/381"} this MO comment
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#magnetic_monopoles Magnetic monopoles
          %p
            When
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundles"} line bundles
            are regarded as models for the topological structure underlying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            the Hopf fibration is often called “the
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+monopole"} magnetic monopole
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
            homotopically as being the 3-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            with origin removed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 - \{0\}
            and think of this as being 3-dimensional physical space with a unit point
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
            at the origin removed. The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            away from the origin is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            on the corresponding Hopf fibration bundle.
          %h3#ktheory K-theory
          %p
            In complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            which generates the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_U(S^2)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi H
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2 = 2 \cdot H - 1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H-1)^2 = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{-1} = 2- H
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+generator"} Bott generator
          %p
            A succinct formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+periodicity"} Bott periodicity
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+K-theory"} complex K-theory
            is that for a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            is that of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(S^2 \times X) \cong K(S^2) \otimes K(X)
          %p
            (It would be interesting to see whether this can be proved by internalizing the (classically easy) calculation for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(S^2)
            to the topos of sheaves over
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The Hopf fibrations over other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            also figure in the more complicated case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+K-theory"} real K-theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_O
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(B O)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+orthogonal+group"} stable orthogonal group
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕆
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+construction"} Hopf construction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one"} Hopf invariant one
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopfion"} Hopfion
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+Hopf+fibration"}> real Hopf fibration
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+Hopf+fibration"} octonionic Hopf fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+construction+in+homotopy+type+theory"} Hopf construction in homotopy type theory
          %h2#References References
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li#Hopf31
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heinz+Hopf"}> Heinz Hopf
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Über die Abbildungen der dreidimensionalen Sphäre auf die Kugelfläche
                %strong 104
                (1931) 637–665 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01457962"}> doi:10.1007/BF01457962
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Hopf35
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heinz+Hopf"}> Heinz Hopf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Über die Abbildungen von Sphären auf Sphäre niedrigerer Dimension
                %strong 25
                1 (1935) 427-440 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/212801"}> eudml:212801
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              Saifuddin Syed,
              %em Group structure on spheres and the Hopf fibration
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SyedHopfFibration.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Gluck"}> Herman Gluck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Warner"} Frank Warner
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chung+Tao+Yang"} Chung Tao Yang
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Division algebras, fibrations of spheres by great spheres and the topological determination of space by the gross behavior of its geodesics
                %strong 50
                4 (1983) 1041-1076 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.dmj/1077303489"}> euclid:dmj/1077303489
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#GluckWarnerZiller86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Gluck"}> Herman Gluck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Warner"} Frank Warner
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Ziller"} Wolfgang Ziller
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of the Hopf fibrations
                %strong 32
                (1986), 173-198 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/266548925_The_geometry_of_the_Hopf_fibrations"}> ResearchGate
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GluckWarnerZiller-HopfFibrations.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Frankel"}> Theodore Frankel
                , §22.4c in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Geometry+of+Physics+-+An+Introduction"} The Geometry of Physics - An Introduction
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139061377"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139061377
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ucsd.edu/~tfrankel/"} website
                with errata and preface for 3rd edition&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Lyons03
              %p
                David W. Lyons:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Elementary Introduction to the Hopf Fibration
                %strong 76
                2 (2003) 87-98 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/3219300"}> doi:10.2307/3219300
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/3219300"} jstor:3219300
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.01642"} arXiv:2212.01642
            %li#Treisman09
              %p
                Zachary Treisman:
                %em A young person’s guide to the Hopf fibration
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0908.1205"}> arXiv:0908.1205
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
                \:
                %em A visualization of the Hopf fibration
                (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://nilesjohnson.net/hopf.html"}> webpage
                , video:
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/AKotMPGFJYk"} YT
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://chiasme.wordpress.com/2014/01/04/third-homotopy-group-of-the-sphere-and-hopf-fibration/"} Third homotopy group of the sphere and Hopf fibration
                (2014)
          %p
            and via the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+theorem"} Pontrjagin theorem
          %ul
            %li#Kosinski93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoni+Kosinski"}> Antoni Kosinski
              , p. 185 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential manifolds
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/kosinski.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/pure-and-applied-mathematics/vol/138/suppl/C"} ISBN:978-0-12-421850-5
          %p
            Formulation in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/homotopytypetheory/show/HomePage"}> HoTT Wiki
